The checksums must DIFFER between first order and each higher-order arm. For the ACTION the
reason is sharper than for the residual: the correction is deferred, so an action that was
not differentiated through it is EXACTLY the first-order action -- an identical checksum
means the exact term never reached the kernel and the row is first order measured twice.
ho_unlim_lagged is the arm that SHOULD match first_order, and is included as that control.

